{%- comment -%}
  «איפה צריך אור?» — the choosing table.

  This section exists because of a gap measured on the live page, not because
  the homepage wanted another block. The brand's whole position is «the narrow
  specialist who also tells you what does NOT suit you» and the hero opens with
  «מה מתאים ומה לא» — but the guidance backing that promise sat at 5100px of a
  6673px page, 76% of the way down. Everything above it was catalogue. A page
  that promises a guide and delivers a bazaar is the same page the five
  competitors already run; the only difference was that this catalogue was
  tidier.

  Nothing here is newly claimed. Every place, every job and every «not for»
  line is lifted from two pages this store already publishes:

    /pages/guide-garden-lighting  — «01 · איפה צריך אור?», the four places;
                                    «02 · מה האור צריך לעשות?», the three jobs;
                                    «03 · איזה מקור חשמל מתאים?», the negatives.
    /pages/why-solar-lighting     — «עדיף פתרון אחר כאשר», the negatives again.

  That sourcing is the point, not a formality. The first principle on «מי אנחנו»
  reads «כאשר מידע אינו מאומת, איננו צריכים להציג אותו כעובדה» — a "not for"
  written fresh for a homepage block would be a claim with nothing under it,
  and it would be the easiest of all claims to be wrong about. If either guide
  is ever rewritten, these defaults have to move with it.

  Night ground on purpose. The page runs hero (night) → terms (paper) →
  catalogue (paper), so the two grounds had stopped alternating and night — the
  scene the product actually lives in — had fallen to under a third of the page.
  This section sits between terms and catalogue and puts the alternation back.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section id="elmsnest-home-places" class="en-places" dir="rtl" aria-labelledby="en-places-title-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="en-places__wrap">

    <header class="en-places__intro">
      <h2 id="en-places-title-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <div class="en-places__lede">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    <div class="en-places__table">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- assign place = block.settings.collection -%}
        {%- if place != blank and place.products_count > 0 -%}
          <a class="en-place" href="{{ place.url }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>

            <span class="en-place__name">
              {%- comment -%}
                The label is written per block rather than taken from the
                collection title. A collection is named for what it holds;
                this column is named for where the buyer is standing, and
                those are not the same sentence. The link underneath still
                goes to the collection, and the count below is the real one.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <strong>{{ block.settings.place_label | default: place.title }}</strong>
              <span class="en-place__count"><bdi dir="ltr">{{ place.products_count }}</bdi> {{ section.settings.count_word }}</span>
            </span>

            <span class="en-place__job">
              <span class="en-place__field">{{ section.settings.job_label }}</span>
              <span class="en-place__value">{{ block.settings.job }}</span>
            </span>

            {%- comment -%}
              The negative column. This is the one thing on the homepage a
              bazaar cannot copy, and it is the reason the section earns its
              height — so it is a column of equal width to the job, never a
              footnote under it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="en-place__not">
              <span class="en-place__field">{{ section.settings.not_label }}</span>
              <span class="en-place__value">{{ block.settings.not_for }}</span>
            </span>

            <span class="en-place__go" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.guide_label != blank -%}
      <div class="en-places__guide">
        <a href="{{ section.settings.guide_url | default: pages['guide-garden-lighting'].url }}">
          {{ section.settings.guide_label }} <span aria-hidden="true">←</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
.en-places,.en-places *{box-sizing:border-box}
.en-places{
  --rule:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.30);
  --rule-soft:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.18);
  direction:rtl;padding:clamp(52px,6.4vw,80px) 0 clamp(56px,6.6vw,84px);
  background:rgb(var(--en-night));color:rgb(var(--en-ink));
  scroll-margin-top:90px
}
.en-places__wrap{width:min(1200px,100%);margin-inline:auto;padding-inline:clamp(18px,4vw,40px)}

.en-places__intro{max-width:46rem;margin-bottom:clamp(26px,3.4vw,38px)}
.en-places__intro h2{
  margin:0;color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important;
  font-size:clamp(32px,4.4vw,52px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:normal;
  text-wrap:balance
}
.en-places__lede{margin-top:13px;color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.78);font-size:clamp(16px,1.7vw,18px);line-height:1.5}
.en-places__lede p{margin:0;color:inherit!important}

/* A ruled schedule, closed on all four sides, so it reads as one instrument
   face rather than four cards that happen to be adjacent. Same construction
   as the hero's place index and the rating plate - this sheet has exactly one
   way of drawing a table and this is it. */
.en-places__table{border:1px solid var(--rule);border-block-end:0}

.en-place{
  display:grid;
  /* name | job | not-for | arrow. The negative gets the same width as the
     job because it carries the same weight in the decision - narrowing it
     would quietly turn the store's one differentiator into a caveat. */
  grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.82fr) minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(0,1.5fr) auto;
  align-items:start;gap:clamp(14px,1.6vw,22px);
  padding:clamp(15px,1.7vw,20px) clamp(16px,2vw,24px);
  border-block-end:1px solid var(--rule);
  color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important;text-decoration:none;
  transition:background-color .18s ease
}
/* No lift and no shadow - the ground tints and the arrow moves, which is the
   whole hover vocabulary on this sheet. */
.en-place:hover{background:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.06)}
.en-place:focus-visible{outline:3px solid rgb(var(--en-ink));outline-offset:-3px}

.en-place__name{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;min-width:0}
.en-place__name strong{
  color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important;
  font-size:clamp(18px,1.9vw,22px);font-weight:700;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:normal;
  text-wrap:balance
}
.en-place__count{color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.60);font-size:13px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

.en-place__job,.en-place__not{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;min-width:0}
/* The field label, same role as a rating-plate dt: it names the measurement
   above its value. Hebrew has no case distinction, so the whole eyebrow
   effect has to come from weight and tracking. */
.en-place__field{
  color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.55);
  font-size:12px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:.04em
}
.en-place__value{color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.86);font-size:15px;line-height:1.45}
/* The negative is set on its own ruled ground rather than in a warning
   colour. There is no red on this sheet, and there should not be: this is
   not an error state, it is a specification - the condition under which the
   answer is no. */
.en-place__not{
  padding-inline-start:clamp(14px,1.8vw,22px);
  border-inline-start:1px solid var(--rule-soft)
}
.en-place__not .en-place__value{color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.74)}

.en-place__go{
  align-self:center;color:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.70);font-size:18px;
  transition:transform .18s ease,color .18s ease
}
.en-place:hover .en-place__go{color:rgb(var(--en-ink));transform:translateX(-3px)}

.en-places__guide{display:flex;margin-top:clamp(24px,3vw,34px)}
.en-places__guide a{
  display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
  min-height:52px;padding:12px 28px;border-radius:0;
  border:1px solid rgb(var(--en-ink)/.58);
  background:transparent;color:rgb(var(--en-ink))!important;
  text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:16px;
  transition:background-color .18s ease,border-color .18s ease
}
.en-places__guide a:hover{border-color:rgb(var(--en-ink));background:rgb(var(--en-ink)/.08)}
.en-places__guide a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid rgb(var(--en-ink));outline-offset:3px}

/* Four columns to two: the name keeps its own row and the two fields sit
   side by side under it, so the job/not-for pairing survives the fold. */
@media(max-width:1050px){
  .en-place{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:12px clamp(16px,2.2vw,24px)}
  /* The place name and its count read as one line here rather than two: at
     this width the count is a qualifier on the name, not a field of its own. */
  .en-place__name{grid-column:1;grid-row:1;flex-direction:row;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 10px}
  .en-place__go{grid-column:2;grid-row:1;align-self:start;padding-block-start:2px}
  .en-place__job{grid-column:1 / -1;grid-row:2}
  .en-place__not{grid-column:1 / -1;grid-row:3;padding-inline-start:0;padding-block-start:12px;border-inline-start:0;border-block-start:1px solid var(--rule-soft)}
}
@media(max-width:749px){
  .en-places__wrap{padding-inline:16px}
  .en-place{padding:18px 16px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .en-place,.en-place__go,.en-places__guide a{transition:none}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ElmsNest places",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "כותרת", "default": "איפה צריך אור?" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "intro", "label": "פתיח", "default": "<p>בחרו את האזור הקרוב ביותר לצורך שלכם. לכל מקום — מה שמתאים, ומה שלא.</p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "job_label", "label": "תווית עמודה: תפקיד האור", "default": "מה האור צריך לעשות" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "not_label", "label": "תווית עמודה: לא מתאים", "default": "לא מתאים כאשר" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "count_word", "label": "מילת הספירה", "default": "מוצרים" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "guide_label", "label": "כפתור המדריך", "default": "למדריך המלא לבחירת תאורה" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "guide_url", "label": "קישור המדריך", "info": "ברירת מחדל: מדריך לבחירת תאורה לגינה" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "place",
      "name": "מקום",
      "limit": 4,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "קולקציה" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "place_label", "label": "שם המקום", "info": "איפה הקונה עומד — לא בהכרח שם הקולקציה" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "job", "label": "מה האור צריך לעשות", "info": "מתוך «02 · מה האור צריך לעשות?» במדריך המפורסם" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "not_for", "label": "לא מתאים כאשר", "info": "חובה לצטט מעמוד מפורסם — «למה תאורה סולארית?» או המדריך. אל תנסחו מחדש." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "ElmsNest places",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "place" },
        { "type": "place" },
        { "type": "place" },
        { "type": "place" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
